    "State arbitrary measure/sample space, no mass normalization or probability assumption for these interfaces. Preserve mass-two identity integral2 and counting-measure infinite branch as nonprobability canaries, not Jensen probability instances.",
    "Explain total lower integrals need no supplied function measurability; signedExpectation is total EReal arithmetic. Legitimate signed-integral interpretation needs appropriate measurability and at least one finite part; both infinite yields formal bottom in this library and is not a valid signed expectation.",
    "State actual Integrable real f includes a.e. strong measurability and finite norm integral for the two finite-part results and Bochner compatibility. Do not extend compatibility to nonintegrable Bochner default zero.",
